{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the congregation lifted up their voice… and the people wept.</b> It says <b>the people</b>, and it was not sufficient [to say] that those who raised their voice remembered [it], meaning that not all of the congregation wept on that night, but only a part of them, even though in the general sense all of them raised their voice to the words of the spies who went to great lengths to frighten them." "It further explains according to the words of the Sages of blessed memory (Sotah 35a; Ta'anit 29a), who said as follows: The Holy One, blessed be He, said: You wept a weeping for nothing — I will fix for you a weeping for generations. End quote. And this is the statement of the verse <b>and the whole congregation lifted up their voice</b> etc., meaning that this was then, and this caused the people weeping on that night for generations. And if the verse had said ״וַיִּבְכּוּ בַּלַּיְלָה״ [and they wept in the night], the matter would have reverted to the aforementioned congregation who heard the words of the spies."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:45.090747646Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}